==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|enm|culpable}}, from {{der|en|fro|culpable}}, from {{der|en|la|culpabilis||blameworthy}}, from {{m|la|culpare||to blame, condemn}}, from {{m|la|culpa||fault, crime, mistake}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkʌlpəbəl/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-culpable.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[merit|Meriting]] [[condemnation]], [[censure]] or [[blame]], especially as something [[wrong]], [[harmful]] or [[injurious]]; [[blameworthy]], [[guilty]].
#: {{ux|en|I am '''culpable''' for stealing your money.}}

